rows.en:
Since then, I still haven't woken from my dream.
And without ever waking from that dream, I'm now living in reality.
Where and how I strayed from the path, I don't know, but the world I'm in now is different somehow.{p}

After the six vanished that day, I just stood there in a daze in front of the old school building.
Once the morning sun had fully shown its face and I could hear the birds singing, people began to appear here and there.
And then the same old everyday life began, unchanged as ever.{p}

That's right.
There's no point sitting at home thinking about it like this.
Holding a faint hope that I might be able to confirm whether what I saw that time was real or a dream, I headed for the school.{p}

And after I got home, I thought it over again.
Maybe people from a world different from ours live in that old school building.
A world completely separate from the one where we live our lives like this.{p}

Come to think of it, I had a mountain of summer homework.
If I didn't do it now, I'd be the one suffering later.
I might as well get at least a little of it out of the way.{p}

No way★
Am I hearing things?
There's no way I could be hearing this voice here.{p}

"Man, what a thickheaded guy."
Another voice came from the other side of the room.
This voice...{p}
